## Design decisions

<!-- Describe the key architectural choices here after the
     LLM polish pass adds project-specific context. -->

- **Why this structure**: the subsystem isolates
  {{ title | lower }} concerns from the rest of the
  codebase, making it possible to swap implementations
  or add backends without touching callers.

{% if public_classes and public_classes | length > 1 %}
- **Class separation**: each class owns a single
  responsibility; they compose rather than inherit to
  keep the dependency graph shallow.
{% endif %}

